    and then computed before the next one is touched, so the first failing
    element wins. That holds across layers. A well-formed element 0 that fails on
    business grounds is reported before a malformed element 1, because the real
    domain code is the true outcome of a request while `invalid-batch-item` only
    says 'this entry is not a request' -- see the public example
    earlier-domain-before-later-shape in SPEC.md:30.

    Within the pass the first failure ends the batch with that element's own
    error code and index: G3 allows no partial results, so nothing computed
    before it is reported. Unlike the single request path, `request` may be any
    object here and non-objects are simply `invalid-batch` rather than
    `invalid-request`.

