    """Comparable identity of one element for retry detection.

    Compared against the *normalized* fields, not the raw object: absent keys are
    filled with their business defaults first, so `retain` omitted and
    `retain: []` are the same request, and an absent `depends_on` inside a change
    cannot fake a difference either. Inputs the journal accepts are shapes that
    read identically when re-validated, so normalizing through those same readers
    cannot invent a conflict.
    """
